'''Padmé's Apartment'''<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|padmes-apartment|Padmé's Apartment}}</ref> was the suite [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] lived in on [[Coruscant]] after her term as [[Monarch of Naboo|Queen]] of [[Naboo]] was concluded and she instead became the [[planet]]'s [[Senator|representative]] in the [[Galactic Senate]].<ref name="Episode II" /> It was located in a high-rise,<ref name="Databank" /> high-security [[Senate apartment complex]] in the upscale [[Federal District]], one of many apartment buildings occupied by diplomatic staff from the millions of [[star system]]s enfranchised in the Senate.<ref name="Complete Locations" /> Although situated at the top of a grand apartment block and lavish by most standards, it was modest compared to many senatorial homes, and lacked advanced security features.<ref name="Complete VD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:Gioconda-Amidala.png|thumb|left|250px|Senator Amidala during a quiet moment in her apartment.]]
During the [[Separatist Crisis]], Amidala was subjected to a series of [[Plot to assassinate Senator Amidala|assassination attempts]], the last of which saw [[Zam Wesell]] smuggle two [[poison]]ous [[kouhun]]s into her bedroom, which were [[Death|killed]] by one of her [[Jedi]] [[bodyguard]]s, [[Anakin Skywalker]]. After her other Jedi guardian, [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], broke one of her [[Viewport|windows]] to chase after the [[ASN-121]] [[assassin droid]] that had deployed the kouhuns, the [[INS-444|window installer droid]] [[Mick]] was dispatched to install a replacement viewport, while the [[CLE-004 window cleaning droid]] [[Buffy]] cleaned up any remaining mess.<ref name="Episode II" />

[[Wedding of Anakin Skywalker and Padmé Amidala|Skywalker and Amidala were married]] on Naboo following the [[First Battle of Geonosis]].<ref name="Episode II" /> The [[Clone Wars]] kept the two apart, however, as Amidala served as a [[senator]] on Coruscant, and Skywalker was a [[Jedi General]] leading the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] in the war. Following a tour of duty, Skywalker returned to Coruscant and entered the apartment with dinner for him and Amidala. He was greeted by their [[protocol droid]], [[C-3PO]], and shared a happy reunion with Amidala. As he entered he referred to the apartment as their "home," and when Amidala noticed he replied there wasn't another name for it. The two shared the evening.<ref name="Senate Spy" />

The apartment was among the meeting places of the [[Delegation of 2,000]], the group of senators Amidala belonged to who plotted to remove [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] from power.<ref name="Padmé Databank biography">{{Databank|padm-amidala-biography-gallery|Padmé Amidala Biography Gallery}}</ref>

Following Amidala's [[death]] and Anakin Skywalker's transformation into [[Darth]] Vader, the senator's apartment was sealed, with a large, tri-dimensional representation of her face blocking the entrance. Many years later, shortly after his [[Duel on Cloud City|duel]] on [[Cloud City]] with his estranged son [[Luke Skywalker]], Vader forced his way into the apartment, accompanied by the [[forensics droid]] [[ZED-6-7]].<ref name="Vader 1">[[Darth Vader (2020) 1|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 1]]</ref>

